  "query_preview": "/Through Friday/...\nIssued at 1145 PM MDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nOnce again will be dealing with areas of dense later tonight thru \nSat morning over portions of the plains and I-25 Corridor. Timing of \nits development, closer to nrn areas of the I-25 Corridor and over \nWeld county, is still a bit uncertain.  However, believe it will \nbegin developing around 09z and then spread south into the Denver \nMetro by 11z or so.  Fog will likely last thru 16z and then \ngradually lift in most areas. \n\nMeanwhile, for the rest of Sat, a disturbance embedded in SW flow \naloft will move across the higher terrain by midday.  This feature \nwill bring a chc of showers to portions of the higher terrain as it \nmoves across.  Over the plains, expect mainly dry conditions with \nhighs in the mid 50's to lower 60's.\n\nLooking ahead to Sun, the ECMWF and GFS have an elongated upper \nlevel trough moving into the nrn Rockies and Great Basin by late Sun \naftn. Ahead of this feature, rather stg SSW flow aloft will be over \nthe area with an influx of subtropical moisture.  For most of the \nday, the best chc of precip will stay to the west but by late aftn \nshould see an increasing chc of showers over the higher terrain. \nAcross the plains, sfc low pres will extend from ern WY into ern CO \nwith gusty southerly winds by aftn. \n\nFor Sun night into Mon, the elongated upper level trough will move \neastward with a couple pieces of energy associated with it. One \npiece of energy will move into the Dakota's while the 2nd piece of \nenergy tracks across srn CO/nrn NM.  As the main upper level trough \nand associated QG ascent moves across will see rain and snow over \nthe higher terrain Sun night into Mon.  Over nern CO, a cold front \nwill move across Mon morning with gusty NNW winds behind it. QG \nfields still show favorable mid level ascent across the plains thru \nthe aftn so will keep in a good chc of showers over the plains. \nHowever, the downslope NNW winds may reduce precip chances closer to \nthe I-25 Corridor.    \n\nBy Mon night, the main upper level trough will move east of the area \nwith drier air moving in behind the system.  Will continue to see a \ngood chc of showers Mon evening mainly over the east central plains. \nHowever, by late Mon evening should see precip gradually end.\n\nOn Tue, an upper level ridge will begin to build into the area with \ndry conditions and near seasonal temperatures.  Looking ahead to the \nmiddle part of next week, there is considerable uncertainty as to \nwhether another system will affect the area or not.  The latest GFS \ntracks this system across the nrn Rockies while the ECMWF has it \nmoving across Colorado.",
